  kicker="From orbit · what one radar image can show, and what it has not"
  current="satellite"
  lede="Can one satellite radar image show chambers under the ground? The real ICEYE passes over Giza are simulated over ground whose contents are known, and the published method and a stricter reconstruction of it are run on real and simulated images beside controls. The methods tested do not show chambers, while single images can measure strong vibration of bright targets. Where this rests on models, and what would test it, is set out below."
